questions.question_text:
A cable runs from $P$ on one bank of a $24$ km wide channel to a station $S$ on the opposite bank, $30$ km downstream from the point $Q$ directly opposite $P$.
Underwater cable costs $\$65\,000$ per km and cable along the bank costs $\$25\,000$ per km.
The cable crosses to a point $x$ km from $Q$, then runs along the bank to $S$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (Q) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P) at (0,4.32);
\coordinate (M) at (2.9,0);
\coordinate (S) at (5.4,0);
\draw (-0.5,4.32) -- (5.9,4.32);
\draw (-0.5,0) -- (5.9,0);
\draw (Q) -- (P) node[midway, left] {$24$ km};
\draw (P) -- (M);
\draw (Q) -- (M) node[midway, below] {$x$ km};
\draw (M) -- (S) node[midway, below] {$30 - x$ km};
\coordinate (a) at ($(Q)!0.35cm!(S)$);
\coordinate (b) at ($(Q)!0.35cm!(P)$);
\draw (a) -- ($(a)+(b)-(Q)$) -- (b);
\node[above] at (P) {$P$};
\node[above left] at (Q) {$Q$};
\node[below right] at (S) {$S$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the value of $x$ that minimises the total cost.
